    "title": "Trump Cuts USAID Funding to NGOs",
    "text": "• Former President Donald Trump made cuts to USAID funding for non-governmental organizations (NGOs).\n• The decision to cut funding was part of a broader strategy to reduce government spending.\n• USAID is responsible for administering civilian foreign aid and development assistance.\n• The cuts have raised concerns among various NGOs about their ability to operate and provide services.\n• Supporters of the cuts argue that it encourages self-sufficiency among recipient countries.\n• Critics claim that reduced funding could lead to increased humanitarian crises and instability.",
